---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { manifestEntry } from '../lib/seo/pages.ts';
const path = '/editorial-policy/';
const entry = manifestEntry(path);
---

<BaseLayout
  title={entry?.title ?? ''}
  description={entry?.description ?? ''}
  path={path}
  indexable={entry?.indexable ?? false}
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Editorial policy', path },
  ]}
>
  <div>
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      How rules get onto this site, and what our review does and does not amount to.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="notice notice--warning">
    <p class="notice__title">No tax professional has reviewed this site</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
      The review described below is a software and data review carried out by the people who build
      the site. It is not a professional tax review, and nothing here has been checked or approved
      by an accountant, tax adviser, or lawyer. If we ever obtain professional review, this page
      will say so and name who did it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="process">
    <h2 id="process">How a rule gets published</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        The rule is read from the tax authority that publishes it. Not from another calculator, not
        from a news article, not from a summary.
      </li>
      <li>
        The figures are entered into a versioned ruleset file alongside the source URL and the date
        they were checked.
      </li>
      <li>
        Tests are written from the authority's own worked examples where they exist, and
        hand-calculated with the workings recorded where they do not.
      </li>
      <li>
        Every band boundary is tested immediately below, at, and immediately above the threshold,
        along with allowances, caps, tapers, and credits.
      </li>
      <li>Someone other than the person who entered the data reviews the diff.</li>
      <li>
        Only then is the ruleset marked published, which is what allows its pages to be indexed.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      A source page changing does not change our figures automatically. There is a monthly automated
      check that raises the question, but a person answers it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="withhold">
    <h2 id="withhold">When we withhold rather than estimate</h2>
    <p>
      If a rule cannot be implemented confidently from an official source, the affected feature is
      marked unsupported and its pages are kept out of search results. This is enforced by the build
      rather than by anyone remembering: a page that fails the quality gate is either not emitted at
      all or emitted with a noindex directive, and it cannot appear in a sitemap.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same applies to combinations we do not model. Selecting an option the rules do not cover
      produces a visible warning, never a plausible-looking guess.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="pages">
    <h2 id="pages">What makes a page worth publishing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not create pages to increase a URL count. A page is published only if it runs a real
      calculation, answers a distinct question, exposes its assumptions, and says something specific
      to its own subject. Salary pages exist for a curated list of amounts held in a single reviewed
      file — not for every number between them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Near-identical pages produced by swapping a city, a currency, or a word are not published at
      all, regardless of what they might rank for.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ads">
    <h2 id="ads">Advertising and independence</h2>
    <p>
      This site is funded by display advertising. Advertising is never allowed to change a
      calculation, a recommendation, or which pages exist. Ad placements are fixed in the page
      layout, are labelled, and are never positioned where they could be mistaken for a result, a
      form control, or a source link. At the time of writing no ads are enabled at all.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p><a href="/corrections/">Found an error? Here is how to report it →</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
